      "title": "Gas temperature falls rapidly under the sprays",
      "description": "Hot gas (e.g. several hundred °C from an incinerator or reactor) is cooled within a short distance to near its adiabatic saturation temperature as the spray water evaporates. Rapid quenching protects downstream equipment and limits the time spent in the temperature window where dioxins/furans can re-form (roughly 200–400 °C) in waste incineration.",
